        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: incomplete—event evidence unavailable\n\nI confirmed the relevant work order and September Pending Close time, but **cannot determine whether a late-created event exists or evaluate its accounting status** from the records available to my analyst role.\n\n| Requested item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | Sep-25 (`PER-COST-2025-09`) |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** — no timezone offset supplied |\n| Source transaction ID | Unavailable |\n| Event amount | Unavailable |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Minutes late | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\nThe authorized task records contain no cost-event rows. Supporting records returned “not staged” and are restricted to the records-custodian role. I requested an authorized event extract, but none was supplied. **This evidence gap does not establish that no late event occurred.**\n\n### Oracle policy\n\nOracle’s supplied 26B documentation states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\n*Source: Oracle Supply Chain Cost Management 26B, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225.*\n\nNo database records were changed. The partial report was submitted with status **“needs_evidence”**, and the audit result and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_e2c367da060d/audit-report.json`.",
